/IXServicePortIF/findFirstDocMasks.description:
This function allows to find docMasks by their name, id, guid, packageguid or packagelevelguid
 properties. Wildcards can be used as defined in the session options, see {@link SessionOptionsC#DB_WILDCARDS}.
 Example:

 <pre>
 <code class="example">
 FindDocMaskInfo findMask = new FindDocMaskInfo();
 findMask.setMaskIdsOrNames(Arrays.asList("testName", "testName2", "testNam*"));
 int idx = 0, max = 10;
 FindResult fr = conn.ix().findFirstDocMasks(findMask, max);
 try {
   while (true) {
     for (String maskName : fr.getDocMasks().values()) {
       // process docMask object
     }

     if (!fr.isMoreResults()) break;

     idx += fr.getDocMasks.length;
     fr = conn.ix().findNextDocMasks(fr.getSearchId(), idx, max);
   }
 }
 catch (RemoteException e) {
   // process exception
   throw e;
 }
 finally {
   conn.ix().findClose(fr.getSearchId());
 }
 </code>
 </pre>

/IXServicePortIF/findFirstUsers.description:
This function allows to find users by their name, description, or one of their
 properties. Wildcards can be used as defined in the session options, see
 {@link SessionOptionsC#DB_WILDCARDS}.
 Example:

 <pre>
 <code class="example">
 FindUserInfo findUserInfo = new FindUserInfo();
 findUserInfo.setName("testFind?sers-*");
 int idx = 0, max = 100;
 FindResult fr = conn.ix().findFirstUsers(findUserInfo, max);
 try {
   while (true) {
     for (UserName userName : fr.getUserNames().values()) {
       // process userName object
     }

     if (!fr.isMoreResults()) break;

     idx += fr.getUserNames().length;
     fr = conn.ix().findNextUsers(fr.getSearchId(), idx, max);
   }
 }
 catch (RemoteException e) {
   // process exception
   throw e;
 }
 finally {
   conn.ix().findClose(fr.getSearchId());
 }
 </code>
 </pre>
 Additionally, FindResult#sortedResult returns a sorted list of either UserInfo or UserName
 objects, depending on {@link FindUserInfo#returnUserInfoMap}.

extending.description:
Aspect association which will be extended.
Optionally set this field to the name of an other AspectAssoc in order
 to extend it. That other AspectAssoc must be present on the same mask. By extending another AspectAssoc, the
 associated {@link Aspect}s gets merged together on this mask. If this field is set, this AspectAssoc must have the
 same {@link #cardinality} as the extending AspectAssoc.

 <p>
 To give an example let's assume we have a given {@link DocMask} that stores orders and has an {@link AspectAssoc}
 "OrderPosition" that is associated with an {@link Aspect} "OrderPosition". You want to add a new {@link AspectLine}
 to the order position but you do not want to modify the given {@link DocMask}.
 </p>

 <pre>{@code
 // create an aspect line that extends a position of an order by a transport restriction
 AspectLine transportRestriction = new AspectLine();
 transportRestriction.setKey("TransportRestriction");
 transportRestriction.setDisplayName("Transport restriction");
 transportRestriction.setType(AspectLineC.TYPE_TEXT);

 // create and save an aspect containing the line obove
 List<AspectLine> extensionLines = new ArrayList<>();
 extensionLines.add(transportRestriction);

 Aspect orderPositionExtension = ixConnect.ix().createAspect("OrderPositionExtension", extensionLines);
 orderPositionExtension.setId(ixConnect.ix().checkinAspect(orderPositionExtension));

 // create an aspect association
 AspectAssoc assocOrderPositionsExtension = ixConnect
     .ix()
     .createAspectAssoc("OrderPositionExtension", Integer.toString(orderPositionExtension.getId()),
         Cardinality.MANY);

 // extend the existing AspectAssoc "OrderPosition" by the above AspectAssoc "OrderPositionExtension"
 invoiceExtension.setExtending("OrderPosition");
 }
 </pre>

 <p>
 Finally add the {@link AspectAssoc} to a {@link DocMask} that contains the extending {@link AspectAssoc}. Ideally,
 create a new Mask and inherit the {@link AspectAssoc} by setting {@link DocMask#inheritFromMasks}.
 </p>

